<title>AUSTRALIA: AUSTRALIA NAMES NEW SECURITIES AGENCY MEMBERS.</title>
<headline>AUSTRALIA NAMES NEW SECURITIES AGENCY MEMBERS.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Treasurer Peter Costello on Thursday named two new members of the Australian Securities Commission.</p>
<p>Rio Tinto Ltd/Plc managing director of group business services Peter Day would become the commission's new deputy chairman.</p>
<p>Lawyer Jillian Segal, a special counsel with Dunhill Madden Butler, had been also appointed to the commission, Costello said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Segal specialises in environmental and corporate law, Costello said.</p>
<p>Day takes over as deputy chairman from Lynn Ralph, whose term has expired. Segal replaces Bill Robinson, who left the commission to work for the Victorian state government in 1996.</p>
<p>They take up their new positions in October.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
